#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Every function's description and grants, in one place. Regenerates
# functions/<name>/<name>.json; never edit those by hand (bin/fnjson.py, as Forms').
#   table   read        table:rw  + write rows        table:rwd  + delete rows
#   workflow:<name>     start and read its runs       connector:<id>  use it
# No function can be granted schedule.create, a table's public rows, a web
# widget or contact reads, so those are done by the app as the person (the
# app's wire.ts): opening the sign-up and check-in tables, the widget, the
# triggers and the hourly sweep, and checking a sign-up's proven email.
set -euo pipefail
cd "$(dirname "$0")/.."
f() { uv run --no-project python bin/fnjson.py "$@"; }
f early_access_setup_options "What the beta sheet offers: the team's features and products, the person's Mail mailboxes, and PostHog's flags and cohorts when PostHog is connected (its state in words when not)." product feature mail_mailbox connector:posthog
f early_access_setup_save "Keep a beta (only the fields given): its name, page address, intro, feature (made at stage beta when new, with a product when the team has none), flag (posthog, by_hand, none) with key and cohort, usage events, survey, batch size, check-in day, quiet days, sign-up questions, state, the person's mailbox, and what Turn on read back. Writes the Public page row and the shared form row. Safe to run again." early_access_beta:rw early_access_page:rw early_access_settings:rw product:rw feature:rw form:rw early_access_signup
f early_access_on_signup "A sign-up landed (the early-access-signup trigger, with row_author): from a contact who confirmed an email, for an open beta, makes or updates the tester (one per person per beta), says Waiting on their status page, and counts the sign-up in the shared form row." early_access_signup:rw early_access_beta early_access_tester:rw early_access_status:rw form:rw company company_domain
f early_access_fit "How well a waiting person fits a beta. brief: the facts the Lemma knows (sign-up answers, an open deal, how much they write, conversations and asks about the feature) and one Decisions call (strong, maybe, not_now) with the team's own fit calls as examples. save: the picker's one-line reason, kept only when it names a fact." early_access_tester:rw early_access_beta deal person person_handle conversation ask
f early_access_rank "Who to let in next for a beta (beta_id, or beta by name or slug): the people waiting ranked by fit, then how sure, then longest waiting, each with the reason and what they said. Read only; it never lets anyone in." early_access_beta early_access_tester
f early_access_draft "One note to one tester in the person's own mailbox (kind invite, checkin, chase, not_now). start: one early-access-draft run per tester_ids. brief: what the writer needs. save: the writer's text as a Mail draft, never sent. One chase per tester, ever." early_access_tester:rw early_access_beta early_access_settings mail_mailbox mail_settings brand draft:rw workflow:early-access-draft
f early_access_let_in "The app's Let in press, as the person (never an agent or schedule): adds each picked tester to the flag's PostHog static cohort (or marks the flag by hand or none), sets them picked (invited when writing themselves), says You're in on their status page, and records the batch." early_access_tester:rw early_access_beta early_access_batch:rw early_access_status:rw connector:posthog
f early_access_take_out "One tester, by a person's press: take them out of the beta (out of the PostHog cohort, status left, Not this time on their page); or fit to set a member's own fit call; or flag_on to tick a by-hand flag." early_access_tester:rw early_access_beta early_access_status:rw connector:posthog
f early_access_sweep "Every hour, as a beta's owner: usage from PostHog by HogQL (active when used in 7 days; not connected is never inactive), people PostHog now knows added to the cohort, the day-6 check-in and the one chase drafted (never a second), and PostHog survey answers filed as feedback." early_access_beta:rw early_access_tester:rw early_access_signup feedback:rw form:rw draft connector:posthog workflow:early-access-draft
f early_access_on_checkin "A check-in answer landed (the early-access-checkin trigger): ties it to a tester by its ref, files each written answer as feedback about the beta's feature (a blocker when they couldn't use it), and marks them heard from." early_access_checkin:rw early_access_tester:rw early_access_beta feedback:rw
f early_access_on_draft "A Mail draft was sent (the early-access-on-draft trigger, as its sender): when Early access wrote it, the tester is invited, checked in, chased once, or told not this time." draft early_access_tester:rw early_access_beta early_access_status:rw
f early_access_on_reply "A new inbound mail (the early-access-on-reply trigger, as the member whose mail it is): a tester's reply in a thread an Early access note started counts as shared, so its words become feedback, and the tester is heard from." message conversation draft early_access_tester:rw early_access_beta feedback:rw
f early_access_needs_you "What in Early access needs the person, in the shared needs_you list Today reads: one decide item per beta and kind (next batch ready, invites to send, check-ins drafted, quiet notes drafted, new blockers). Resolves what no longer applies." early_access_beta early_access_tester early_access_batch draft feedback needs_you:rw
f early_access_memory "Tells this Lemma's agents that Early access is installed: its block in /memory/AGENTS.md and its guide at /memory/plugins/early-access.md, leaving the team's notes alone. Safe to run again; remove takes both out." /memory:read,write
f early_access_sample_data "load: a sample beta (one feature, 40 made-up people at .example addresses in every state, what they said, one note drafted and never sent). clear: removes only what the sample made." early_access_beta:rwd early_access_page:rwd early_access_tester:rwd early_access_batch:rwd early_access_status:rwd early_access_signup early_access_sample_row:rwd product:rwd feature:rwd feedback:rwd draft:rwd form:rwd
